From 78b49f6992a284c6099fa4660d1e2e34a765a0d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:09:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] perf(sim): B2 G1 core: piece budgets, urgent budget,
 resumable kernels
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The shared pieces of B2 (docs/dev/B2_DESIGN.md §3.1, §4, §10, §11) that the
split infra tasks build on. Nothing calls them yet; results are unchanged.

- scheduler: pieceUnits(usPerUnit, min, budgetMs) / pieceBudgetUs() derive
  chunk sizes from deterministic constants (no clock); setPieceScale /
  withPieceScale are the test hook (1e9 = one piece per stage, 1e-9 = one
  unit per piece). STEP_GUARD 64 -> 256. Urgent steps re-scan for the first
  urgent and due task under one cap per run: INFRA_URGENT_BUDGET (24 est.
  ms) headless, INFRA_URGENT_FRAME_MS (6 real ms) live; the first one always
  runs (pre-B2: 8 steps, no time check). flush() reports whether it drained.
- params: INFRA_PIECE_MS 0.3 (searches, inbound / shop / freight),
  INFRA_PIECE_COLD_MS 0.13 (Building loops and once-per-pass stages; design
  review 2 item 1), the urgent caps; CREDIT_FLOOR moves here unchanged.
- common: BuildingSnapshot (pass-start building list, greedy chunk plan by
  a + b * footprint).
- search: RoadSearchRun / TransitSearchRun (Dial searches resumable at any
  settle count, private bucket queues, budget checked before an entry is
  taken), accumulateRange (backward settle-order ranges), SearchK
  refreshAltBegin / refreshAltRange. The whole-call functions are unchanged.
- graph: GraphBuildRun (road + rail + subway graphs in stages into private
  buffers; publish() reproduces RoadGraph.build / GridGraph.build into the
  live graphs: growth policy, tails, versions).
- transit: StopCollector (collectStops in building / cell chunks),
  copyStopList (StopList.push growth).
- blur / parking: boxHRows, BoxVRun, baseSupplyRange,
  parkingFromBoxesRange, parkingSummaryOf.
- tests: b2Harness (city / field digests, NaN-canonical) and b2Pieces core
  tests: each kernel in random chunks equals its whole-call original.

